   "reason": "Maintainer fixes after the first review (2026-11-18; the maintainers' decision: keep tests/hidden/episodes.json byte-identical, so the 12 episodes, their units, seeds, benches, worklists, fills and credit stay what they were). Frozen files that changed, and why none changes an episode: (1) tests/verify.py: the 9000 s budget is charged to the controller's own time (READY and every reply, plus 0.2 s per image asked for) instead of the wall clock with the grader's simulation and rendering in it; a task error if the sandbox starts anything as the agent's account by itself, and every process of the account must carry the launcher's no_new_privs mark (the verifier image, tests/Dockerfile, runs no desktop session); a numerics fingerprint is checked before grading (tests/numerics_check.py, tests/numerics.json); docstrings. The wire, the probe lock and its schedule, the credit and the set are unchanged. (2) tests/grader_config.json: image_cost_s 0.2 added. (3) lab_sim.py and lab_env.py (tests/ and solution/oracle/, byte-identical): one renderer per image size, kept for the episode's model, instead of one per image (24 images compared with the old path: byte-identical, the sensor noise drawn exactly as before); a development-tree import path removed. (4) box_transport_env.py (both copies): the table's half width in y 0.60 -> 0.80 m, so that the cold rack, whose pose and draw are unchanged, stands on the table. This is the one change that is not bit-neutral for the simulation: with the same contacts, the solver's order of constraints changes with the table's bounding box, and the first state after reset differs by 1.3e-6 (rotor, knob, preloaded tubes); everything else was checked bit-identical on a development episode with the table at 0.60. (5) solution/oracle/wire_world.py: the reference no longer answers a hold when its planning thread has not produced a command within 10 s of wall time; it waits for the command, so its actions are a function of the observations alone. solution/solve.sh, tests/episode.py, tests/units.json and the other reference modules are unchanged. Both images pin OPENBLAS_CORETYPE=Haswell (the simulation's numerics fingerprint is identical on two CPU classes with the pin). Because of (4) the reference's runs cannot repeat step for step; the rule's evidence is its full verify on the made set with the new files: every episode at credit 1.0 again.",
